 ## Background
-The U-Net variant was introduced as an extension of the original 2D U-Net architecture to 3D volumes [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the encoder-decoder structure of 3D CNNs, which stack downsampling and upsampling stages to extract and reconstruct spatial features [S1, unofficial]. The addition of skip connections allows the network to preserve high-resolution information, addressing the blurring effects often seen in standard convolutional networks for volumetric data [G]. It has become a standard architecture for tasks such as microvascular segmentation in cerebrovascular micro-MRI [S1, unofficial].
